IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `aia-definitions`
IMPORT `P3-section-3`

-- P3-art-25: Article 25 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): responsibilities along the AI value chain.
-- Lines 468-490 of the consolidated text. Paragraphs 2 and 4 were replaced by the Omnibus (the passages marked M1 at lines 475-481 and 487); the text as enacted is lines 999-1016 of the base text.
-- Article 2(13) names Articles 9 to 15 and 17 to 25, so Article 25 is among those whose application may be limited for an Article 6(1) system (the gate).
-- OUTPUTS FOR THE OTHER PARTS' SEATS: paragraphs 1 and 3 decide whether a distributor, importer, deployer, other third-party or product manufacturer "shall be considered to be a provider" and "subject to the obligations of the provider under Article 16".
-- A part that asks a question of a provider (Articles 16 to 27 here; Articles 8 to 15, 43, 47 to 49, 72 and 73 elsewhere) must first ask these functions for any party that is not a provider by Article 3(3); this part does not restate those articles.
-- Seams: Article 3(23) is called from the keel (`Art 3(23) the change is a substantial modification`); Article 6 (the classification) is a plain BOOLEAN input (S1 is the route in the `AI system` record, not the classification itself).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE met or deemed; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING not covered (the group does not yet apply, Art 2(13) may limit the Article, a list is not closed, or the paragraph limits itself).

§ `Article 25(1): a distributor, importer, deployer or other third-party considered to be a provider`

-- src:470 | 1. Any distributor, importer, deployer or other third-party shall be considered to be a provider of a high-risk AI system for the purposes of this Regulation and shall be subject to the obligations of the provider under Article 16, in any of the following circumstances:
-- src:471 | (a) they put their name or trademark on a high-risk AI system already placed on the market or put into service, without prejudice to contractual arrangements stipulating that the obligations are otherwise allocated;
-- src:472 | (b) they make a substantial modification to a high-risk AI system that has already been placed on the market or has already been put into service in such a way that it remains a high-risk AI system pursuant to Article 6;
-- src:473 | (c) they modify the intended purpose of an AI system, including a general-purpose AI system, which has not been classified as high-risk and has already been placed on the market or put into service in such a way that the AI system concerned becomes a high-risk AI system in accordance with Article 6.
@ref Art 25(1) (src:470-473)
DECLARE `Art 25(1) what the party has done` HAS
    `the party is a distributor, importer, deployer or other third-party`                                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party puts its name or trademark on a high-risk AI system already placed on the market or put into service`                                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- (a)
    `the party makes a change to the AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b), Art 3(23)
    `the change is foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b), Art 3(23)
    `as a result of the change the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected`                             IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b), Art 3(23)
    `the change results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b), Art 3(23)
    `the AI system remains a high-risk AI system pursuant to Article 6 after the change`                                                                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b)
    `the party modifies the intended purpose of an AI system which has not been classified as high-risk and has already been placed on the market or put into service` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)
    `the AI system concerned becomes a high-risk AI system in accordance with Article 6`                                                                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)

-- Point (a) is "without prejudice to contractual arrangements stipulating that the obligations are otherwise allocated": the deeming does not turn on the contract, so no contractual fact is an input.
@ref Art 25(1)(a) (src:471)
GIVEN `the party` IS AN `Art 25(1) what the party has done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 25(1)(a) the party puts its name or trademark on a high-risk AI system already placed on the market or put into service` MEANS
    `the party`'s `the party puts its name or trademark on a high-risk AI system already placed on the market or put into service`

-- src:472 | (b) they make a substantial modification to a high-risk AI system that has already been placed on the market or has already been put into service in such a way that it remains a high-risk AI system pursuant to Article 6;
@ref Art 25(1)(b) (src:472)
GIVEN `the party` IS AN `Art 25(1) what the party has done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 25(1)(b) the party makes a substantial modification that leaves the system a high-risk AI system` MEANS
        `Art 3(23) the change is a substantial modification`
            (`the party`'s `the party makes a change to the AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service`)
            (`the party`'s `the change is foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider`)
            (`the party`'s `as a result of the change the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected`)
            (`the party`'s `the change results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed`)
    AND `the party`'s `the AI system remains a high-risk AI system pursuant to Article 6 after the change`

-- src:473 | (c) they modify the intended purpose of an AI system, including a general-purpose AI system, which has not been classified as high-risk and has already been placed on the market or put into service in such a way that the AI system concerned becomes a high-risk AI system in accordance with Article 6.
@ref Art 25(1)(c) (src:473)
GIVEN `the party` IS AN `Art 25(1) what the party has done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 25(1)(c) the party modifies the intended purpose so that the AI system becomes a high-risk AI system` MEANS
        `the party`'s `the party modifies the intended purpose of an AI system which has not been classified as high-risk and has already been placed on the market or put into service`
    AND `the party`'s `the AI system concerned becomes a high-risk AI system in accordance with Article 6`

-- "shall be considered to be a provider ... in any of the following circumstances": the circumstances are not closed with "only", so where none holds the answer is NOT covered (NOTHING), not "not a provider" (fork F-25-1-closed in NOTES.md; the other reading is JUST FALSE).
-- src:470 | 1. Any distributor, importer, deployer or other third-party shall be considered to be a provider of a high-risk AI system for the purposes of this Regulation and shall be subject to the obligations of the provider under Article 16, in any of the following circumstances:
@ref Art 25(1) (src:470)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the party` IS AN `Art 25(1) what the party has done`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 25(1) the party is considered to be the provider of the high-risk AI system` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the party`'s `the party is a distributor, importer, deployer or other third-party`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any distributor, importer, deployer or other third-party shall be considered to be a provider"
        ELSE IF       `Art 25(1)(a) the party puts its name or trademark on a high-risk AI system already placed on the market or put into service` `the party`
                   OR `Art 25(1)(b) the party makes a substantial modification that leaves the system a high-risk AI system` `the party`
                   OR `Art 25(1)(c) the party modifies the intended purpose so that the AI system becomes a high-risk AI system` `the party`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "in any of the following circumstances" is not closed with "only"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)

§ `Article 25(2): the initial provider is no longer a provider, and cooperates with the new providers (both versions)`

DECLARE `Art 25(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 25(2) closely cooperate with new providers, make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance`
    `Art 25(2) as amended carry out the particular obligations of points (a) to (c), where relevant`

-- The first subparagraph and the last one (the exception) read the same on both sides of 27 July 2026, so they are encoded once, quoting both texts.
-- Where the circumstances of paragraph 1 do not occur, or the initial provider "has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system", the paragraph does not apply:
-- the answer is JUST FALSE for both (the "Where" that fails and "This paragraph shall not apply": the periods ruling, rule (b), and a flat negative; fork F-when-upon).
-- src:475 | 2. Where the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur, the provider that initially placed the AI system on the market or put it into service shall no longer be considered to be a provider of that specific AI system for the purposes of this Regulation.
-- src:476 | That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance that are required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation, in particular with regard to compliance with the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems.
-- src:477 | In particular, the obligation laid down in the second subparagraph shall include, where relevant for the purposes specified therein, the following:
-- src:478 | (a) making available of technical documentation sufficient to assess compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 16;
-- src:479 | (b) informing the new providers about known limitations and failure modes; and
-- src:480 | (c) providing the new providers with targeted technical access, including for testing and validation.
-- src:481 | This paragraph shall not apply in cases where the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system and therefore does not fall under the obligation to cooperate with the new providers and hand over the documentation.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1008 | 2. Where the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur, the provider that initially placed the AI system on the market or put it into service shall no longer be considered to be a provider of that specific AI system for the purposes of this Regulation. That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance that are required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation, in particular regarding the compliance with the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems. This paragraph shall not apply in cases where the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system and therefore does not fall under the obligation to hand over the documentation.
@ref Art 25(2) first subparagraph (src:475-481) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1008)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 25(2) the initial provider is no longer considered to be a provider of that specific AI system` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur, the provider that initially placed the AI system on the market or put it into service shall no longer be considered to be a provider" (a "where" that fails)
        ELSE IF `the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system`
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph shall not apply in cases where the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)

-- src:476 | That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance that are required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation, in particular with regard to compliance with the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1008 | 2. Where the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur, the provider that initially placed the AI system on the market or put it into service shall no longer be considered to be a provider of that specific AI system for the purposes of this Regulation. That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance that are required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation, in particular regarding the compliance with the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems. This paragraph shall not apply in cases where the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system and therefore does not fall under the obligation to hand over the documentation.
@ref Art 25(2) second subparagraph (src:476) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1008)
DECLARE `Art 25(2) what the initial provider has done` HAS
    `the initial provider has closely cooperated with the new providers`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the initial provider has made available the necessary information`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the initial provider has provided the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN

-- VERSION as enacted (base line 1008). No date and no gate: the dispatcher below never reaches it (Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply only after 27 July 2026), so the text as enacted is tested through this function.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1008 | 2. Where the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur, the provider that initially placed the AI system on the market or put it into service shall no longer be considered to be a provider of that specific AI system for the purposes of this Regulation. That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance that are required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation, in particular regarding the compliance with the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems. This paragraph shall not apply in cases where the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system and therefore does not fall under the obligation to hand over the documentation.
@ref Art 25(2) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1008)
GIVEN `the done` IS AN `Art 25(2) what the initial provider has done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 25(2) as enacted the initial provider has cooperated` MEANS
        `the done`'s `the initial provider has closely cooperated with the new providers`
    AND `the done`'s `the initial provider has made available the necessary information`
    AND `the done`'s `the initial provider has provided the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance that are required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation"

-- VERSION as amended. The second subparagraph reads as enacted ("with regard to compliance" for "regarding the compliance"), and the Omnibus adds a third subparagraph: the obligation "shall include, where relevant ...", points (a) to (c).
-- Each point is owed where it is relevant; one that is not relevant asks nothing.
-- src:477 | In particular, the obligation laid down in the second subparagraph shall include, where relevant for the purposes specified therein, the following:
-- src:478 | (a) making available of technical documentation sufficient to assess compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 16;
-- src:479 | (b) informing the new providers about known limitations and failure modes; and
-- src:480 | (c) providing the new providers with targeted technical access, including for testing and validation.
@ref Art 25(2) as amended third subparagraph (src:477-480)
DECLARE `Art 25(2) the particular obligations of the third subparagraph` HAS
    `making available technical documentation sufficient to assess compliance is relevant for the purposes specified in the second subparagraph`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- (a)
    `the initial provider has made available technical documentation sufficient to assess compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 16` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (a)
    `informing the new providers about known limitations and failure modes is relevant for the purposes specified in the second subparagraph`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b)
    `the initial provider has informed the new providers about known limitations and failure modes`                                                IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b)
    `providing targeted technical access is relevant for the purposes specified in the second subparagraph`                                         IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)
    `the initial provider has provided the new providers with targeted technical access, including for testing and validation`                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)

-- src:476 | That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance that are required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation, in particular with regard to compliance with the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems.
-- src:477 | In particular, the obligation laid down in the second subparagraph shall include, where relevant for the purposes specified therein, the following:
-- src:478 | (a) making available of technical documentation sufficient to assess compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 16;
-- src:479 | (b) informing the new providers about known limitations and failure modes; and
-- src:480 | (c) providing the new providers with targeted technical access, including for testing and validation.
@ref Art 25(2) as amended (src:476-480)
GIVEN `the done` IS AN `Art 25(2) what the initial provider has done`
      `the particulars` IS AN `Art 25(2) the particular obligations of the third subparagraph`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 25(2) as amended the initial provider has cooperated` MEANS
        `the done`'s `the initial provider has closely cooperated with the new providers`
    AND `the done`'s `the initial provider has made available the necessary information`
    AND `the done`'s `the initial provider has provided the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation`
    AND ((NOT `the particulars`'s `making available technical documentation sufficient to assess compliance is relevant for the purposes specified in the second subparagraph`) OR `the particulars`'s `the initial provider has made available technical documentation sufficient to assess compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 16`)
    AND ((NOT `the particulars`'s `informing the new providers about known limitations and failure modes is relevant for the purposes specified in the second subparagraph`) OR `the particulars`'s `the initial provider has informed the new providers about known limitations and failure modes`)
    AND ((NOT `the particulars`'s `providing targeted technical access is relevant for the purposes specified in the second subparagraph`) OR `the particulars`'s `the initial provider has provided the new providers with targeted technical access, including for testing and validation`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information ... In particular, the obligation laid down in the second subparagraph shall include, where relevant for the purposes specified therein, the following"

-- The dispatcher. Where the circumstances of paragraph 1 do not occur, or the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed, the duty to cooperate is not triggered: NOTHING (limited by its own wording; fork F-when-upon).
-- src:475 | 2. Where the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur, the provider that initially placed the AI system on the market or put it into service shall no longer be considered to be a provider of that specific AI system for the purposes of this Regulation.
-- src:476 | That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance that are required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation, in particular with regard to compliance with the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems.
-- src:477 | In particular, the obligation laid down in the second subparagraph shall include, where relevant for the purposes specified therein, the following:
-- src:478 | (a) making available of technical documentation sufficient to assess compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 16;
-- src:479 | (b) informing the new providers about known limitations and failure modes; and
-- src:480 | (c) providing the new providers with targeted technical access, including for testing and validation.
-- src:481 | This paragraph shall not apply in cases where the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system and therefore does not fall under the obligation to cooperate with the new providers and hand over the documentation.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1008 | 2. Where the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur, the provider that initially placed the AI system on the market or put it into service shall no longer be considered to be a provider of that specific AI system for the purposes of this Regulation. That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance that are required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation, in particular regarding the compliance with the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems. This paragraph shall not apply in cases where the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system and therefore does not fall under the obligation to hand over the documentation.
@ref Art 25(2) (src:475-481) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1008)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the done` IS AN `Art 25(2) what the initial provider has done`
      `the particulars` IS AN `Art 25(2) the particular obligations of the third subparagraph`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 25(2) the initial provider has cooperated with the new providers` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF (NOT `the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur`) OR `the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur" and "This paragraph shall not apply in cases where the initial provider has clearly specified"
        ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
             WHEN `as enacted` THEN                                                                  -- VERSION as enacted
                 JUST (`Art 25(2) as enacted the initial provider has cooperated` `the done`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): see the as-enacted function
             WHEN `as amended` THEN                                                                  -- VERSION as amended
                 JUST (`Art 25(2) as amended the initial provider has cooperated` `the done` `the particulars`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): see the as-amended function
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)

-- The regulative rules. No time limit is stated, so no trace reaches a breach. The duty to cooperate is the initial provider's (Role Provider); its extra obligations of the third subparagraph exist only in the text as amended.
-- src:476 | That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance that are required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation, in particular with regard to compliance with the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1008 | 2. Where the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur, the provider that initially placed the AI system on the market or put it into service shall no longer be considered to be a provider of that specific AI system for the purposes of this Regulation. That initial provider shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance that are required for the fulfilment of the obligations set out in this Regulation, in particular regarding the compliance with the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems. This paragraph shall not apply in cases where the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system and therefore does not fall under the obligation to hand over the documentation.
@ref Art 25(2) second subparagraph (src:476) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1008)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 25(2) act`
`Art 25(2) the initial provider's duty to cooperate closely with the new providers` MEANS
    IF       `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
         AND `the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur`
         AND NOT `the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 25(2) closely cooperate with new providers, make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the initial provider did not closely cooperate with the new providers, make available the necessary information and provide the reasonably expected technical access and other assistance"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, the circumstances of paragraph 1 do not occur, or the exception applies
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)

-- src:477 | In particular, the obligation laid down in the second subparagraph shall include, where relevant for the purposes specified therein, the following:
-- src:478 | (a) making available of technical documentation sufficient to assess compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 16;
-- src:479 | (b) informing the new providers about known limitations and failure modes; and
-- src:480 | (c) providing the new providers with targeted technical access, including for testing and validation.
@ref Art 25(2) as amended third subparagraph (src:477-480)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at least one of the particular obligations of points (a) to (c) is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 25(2) act`
`Art 25(2) as amended the initial provider's duty to carry out the particular obligations of points (a) to (c) where relevant` MEANS
    IF       `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
         AND `the circumstances referred to in paragraph 1 occur`
         AND NOT `the initial provider has clearly specified that its AI system is not to be changed into a high-risk AI system`
         AND `at least one of the particular obligations of points (a) to (c) is relevant`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 25(2) as amended carry out the particular obligations of points (a) to (c), where relevant`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the initial provider did not carry out the particular obligations of points (a) to (c) that were relevant"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, the circumstances of paragraph 1 do not occur, the exception applies, or no point is relevant
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)

§ `Article 25(3): the product manufacturer considered to be the provider`

-- src:483 | 3. In the case of high-risk AI systems that are safety components of products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, the product manufacturer shall be considered to be the provider of the high-risk AI system, and shall be subject to the obligations under Article 16 under either of the following circumstances:
-- src:484 | (a) the high-risk AI system is placed on the market together with the product under the name or trademark of the product manufacturer;
-- src:485 | (b) the high-risk AI system is put into service under the name or trademark of the product manufacturer after the product has been placed on the market.
@ref Art 25(3) (src:483-485)
DECLARE `Art 25(3) what is the case` HAS
    `the high-risk AI system is a safety component of a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party is the product manufacturer`                                                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the high-risk AI system is placed on the market together with the product under the name or trademark of the product manufacturer`         IS A BOOLEAN  -- (a)
    `the high-risk AI system is put into service under the name or trademark of the product manufacturer after the product has been placed on the market` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b)

-- Like paragraph 1, the circumstances are not closed with "only": where neither holds the answer is NOT covered (fork F-25-1-closed).
-- src:483 | 3. In the case of high-risk AI systems that are safety components of products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, the product manufacturer shall be considered to be the provider of the high-risk AI system, and shall be subject to the obligations under Article 16 under either of the following circumstances:
-- src:484 | (a) the high-risk AI system is placed on the market together with the product under the name or trademark of the product manufacturer;
-- src:485 | (b) the high-risk AI system is put into service under the name or trademark of the product manufacturer after the product has been placed on the market.
@ref Art 25(3) (src:483-485)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the facts` IS AN `Art 25(3) what is the case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 25(3) the product manufacturer is considered to be the provider of the high-risk AI system` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the facts`'s `the high-risk AI system is a safety component of a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` AND `the facts`'s `the party is the product manufacturer`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of high-risk AI systems that are safety components of products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, the product manufacturer shall be considered to be the provider"
        ELSE IF       `the facts`'s `the high-risk AI system is placed on the market together with the product under the name or trademark of the product manufacturer`
                   OR `the facts`'s `the high-risk AI system is put into service under the name or trademark of the product manufacturer after the product has been placed on the market`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "under either of the following circumstances" is not closed with "only"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)

§ `Article 25(4): the written agreement between the provider and the third party that supplies items used or integrated in a high-risk AI system (both versions)`

DECLARE `Art 25(4) supplied item` IS ONE OF
    `Supplied AI system`
    `Supplied AI model`
    `Supplied tool`
    `Supplied service`
    `Supplied component`
    `Supplied process`
    `Supplied something else`

-- src:487 | 4. The provider of a high-risk AI system and the third party that supplies an AI system, AI model, tools, services, components, or processes that are used or integrated in a high-risk AI system shall, by written agreement, specify the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance based on the generally acknowledged state of the art, in order to enable the provider of the high-risk AI system to fully comply with the obligations set out in this Regulation. This paragraph shall not apply to third parties making accessible to the public tools, services, processes, or components, other than general-purpose AI models, under a free and open-source licence.
