GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the supply` IS AN `Art 25(4) the supply and the agreement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 25(4) the provider and the third party have specified by written agreement the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the supply`'s `the item is used or integrated in a high-risk AI system`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that are used or integrated in a high-risk AI system"
        ELSE IF NOT (`Art 25(4) the item is one the paragraph names on the date asked` `the date asked` `the supply`)
             THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph names "an AI system, [AI model,] tools, services, components, or processes" and does not close the list with "only"
             ELSE IF `Art 25(4) the paragraph does not apply because of the free and open-source carve-out` `the supply`
                  THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph shall not apply to third parties making accessible to the public tools, services, processes, or components, other than general-purpose AI models, under a free and open-source licence"
                  ELSE IF `the supply`'s `the provider and the third party have a written agreement` AND `the supply`'s `the agreement specifies the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance based on the generally acknowledged state of the art, in order to enable the provider to fully comply with the obligations set out in this Regulation`
                       THEN JUST TRUE
                       ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, by written agreement, specify the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance based on the generally acknowledged state of the art, in order to enable the provider of the high-risk AI system to fully comply with the obligations set out in this Regulation"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)

DECLARE `Art 25(4) party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 25(4) provider of the high-risk AI system`
    `Art 25(4) third party that supplies the item`

DECLARE `Art 25(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 25(4) specify by written agreement the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance`

-- The duty is the provider's and the third party's alike ("The provider ... and the third party ... shall, by written agreement, specify"), so one rule per party. No time limit is stated.
-- src:487 | 4. The provider of a high-risk AI system and the third party that supplies an AI system, AI model, tools, services, components, or processes that are used or integrated in a high-risk AI system shall, by written agreement, specify the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance based on the generally acknowledged state of the art, in order to enable the provider of the high-risk AI system to fully comply with the obligations set out in this Regulation. This paragraph shall not apply to third parties making accessible to the public tools, services, processes, or components, other than general-purpose AI models, under a free and open-source licence.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1014 | 4. The provider of a high-risk AI system and the third party that supplies an AI system, tools, services, components, or processes that are used or integrated in a high-risk AI system shall, by written agreement, specify the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance based on the generally acknowledged state of the art, in order to enable the provider of the high-risk AI system to fully comply with the obligations set out in this Regulation. This paragraph shall not apply to third parties making accessible to the public tools, services, processes, or components, other than general-purpose AI models, under a free and open-source licence.
@ref Art 25(4) (src:487) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1014)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the supply` IS AN `Art 25(4) the supply and the agreement`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 25(4) party` `Art 25(4) act`
`Art 25(4) the provider's duty to specify by written agreement` MEANS
    IF       `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
         AND `the supply`'s `the item is used or integrated in a high-risk AI system`
         AND `Art 25(4) the item is one the paragraph names on the date asked` `the date asked` `the supply`
         AND NOT (`Art 25(4) the paragraph does not apply because of the free and open-source carve-out` `the supply`)
    THEN PARTY `Art 25(4) provider of the high-risk AI system`
         MUST `Art 25(4) specify by written agreement the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 25(4) provider of the high-risk AI system` BECAUSE "the provider did not specify by written agreement the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, the item is not used or integrated in a high-risk AI system, is not one the paragraph names, or falls in the carve-out
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)

-- src:487 | 4. The provider of a high-risk AI system and the third party that supplies an AI system, AI model, tools, services, components, or processes that are used or integrated in a high-risk AI system shall, by written agreement, specify the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance based on the generally acknowledged state of the art, in order to enable the provider of the high-risk AI system to fully comply with the obligations set out in this Regulation. This paragraph shall not apply to third parties making accessible to the public tools, services, processes, or components, other than general-purpose AI models, under a free and open-source licence.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1014 | 4. The provider of a high-risk AI system and the third party that supplies an AI system, tools, services, components, or processes that are used or integrated in a high-risk AI system shall, by written agreement, specify the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance based on the generally acknowledged state of the art, in order to enable the provider of the high-risk AI system to fully comply with the obligations set out in this Regulation. This paragraph shall not apply to third parties making accessible to the public tools, services, processes, or components, other than general-purpose AI models, under a free and open-source licence.
@ref Art 25(4) (src:487) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1014)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the supply` IS AN `Art 25(4) the supply and the agreement`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 25(4) party` `Art 25(4) act`
`Art 25(4) the third party's duty to specify by written agreement` MEANS
    IF       `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
         AND `the supply`'s `the item is used or integrated in a high-risk AI system`
         AND `Art 25(4) the item is one the paragraph names on the date asked` `the date asked` `the supply`
         AND NOT (`Art 25(4) the paragraph does not apply because of the free and open-source carve-out` `the supply`)
    THEN PARTY `Art 25(4) third party that supplies the item`
         MUST `Art 25(4) specify by written agreement the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 25(4) third party that supplies the item` BECAUSE "the third party did not specify by written agreement the necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, the item is not used or integrated in a high-risk AI system, is not one the paragraph names, or falls in the carve-out
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)

§ `Article 25(4) second subparagraph: the AI Office and the voluntary model terms (addressed to an official; no seat)`

-- "The AI Office may develop and recommend voluntary model terms ... shall take into account possible contractual requirements ... shall be published and be available free of charge in an easily usable electronic format."
-- It matters to a provider or third party because the terms are voluntary and free: the function says whether the published terms meet the paragraph. Nothing in the paragraph forces a provider or third party to use them.
-- src:489 | The AI Office may develop and recommend voluntary model terms for contracts between providers of high-risk AI systems and third parties that supply tools, services, components or processes that are used for or integrated into high-risk AI systems. When developing those voluntary model terms, the AI Office shall take into account possible contractual requirements applicable in specific sectors or business cases. The voluntary model terms shall be published and be available free of charge in an easily usable electronic format.
@ref Art 25(4) second subparagraph (src:489)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the AI Office has developed voluntary model terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI Office has taken into account possible contractual requirements applicable in specific sectors or business cases` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the voluntary model terms have been published` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the voluntary model terms are available free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the voluntary model terms are available in an easily usable electronic format` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 25(4) the AI Office has met the requirements for the voluntary model terms` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the AI Office has developed voluntary model terms`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The AI Office may develop and recommend voluntary model terms"; the requirements bind terms that have been developed
        ELSE IF       `the AI Office has taken into account possible contractual requirements applicable in specific sectors or business cases`
                  AND `the voluntary model terms have been published`
                  AND `the voluntary model terms are available free of charge`
                  AND `the voluntary model terms are available in an easily usable electronic format`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When developing those voluntary model terms, the AI Office shall take into account possible contractual requirements applicable in specific sectors or business cases. The voluntary model terms shall be published and be available free of charge in an easily usable electronic format"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)

DECLARE `Art 25(4) AI Office body` IS ONE OF
    `Art 25(4) AI Office`

DECLARE `Art 25(4) AI Office act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 25(4) develop and recommend voluntary model terms`
    `Art 25(4) take into account possible contractual requirements applicable in specific sectors or business cases`
    `Art 25(4) publish the voluntary model terms and make them available free of charge in an easily usable electronic format`

-- Developing the terms is a permission ("may"); once it does, taking contractual requirements into account and then publishing are duties. No time limit is stated.
-- src:489 | The AI Office may develop and recommend voluntary model terms for contracts between providers of high-risk AI systems and third parties that supply tools, services, components or processes that are used for or integrated into high-risk AI systems. When developing those voluntary model terms, the AI Office shall take into account possible contractual requirements applicable in specific sectors or business cases. The voluntary model terms shall be published and be available free of charge in an easily usable electronic format.
@ref Art 25(4) second subparagraph (src:489)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 25(4) AI Office body` `Art 25(4) AI Office act`
`Art 25(4) the AI Office's permission to develop and recommend voluntary model terms and its duties once it does` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY `Art 25(4) AI Office`
         MAY `Art 25(4) develop and recommend voluntary model terms`
         HENCE PARTY `Art 25(4) AI Office`
               MUST `Art 25(4) take into account possible contractual requirements applicable in specific sectors or business cases`
               HENCE PARTY `Art 25(4) AI Office`
                     MUST `Art 25(4) publish the voluntary model terms and make them available free of charge in an easily usable electronic format`
                     HENCE FULFILLED
                     LEST BREACH BY `Art 25(4) AI Office` BECAUSE "the voluntary model terms were not published and made available free of charge in an easily usable electronic format"
               LEST BREACH BY `Art 25(4) AI Office` BECAUSE "possible contractual requirements applicable in specific sectors or business cases were not taken into account"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)

§ `Article 25(5): paragraphs 2 and 3 are without prejudice to the protection of intellectual property rights, confidential business information and trade secrets`

-- A saving clause, not a duty: it keeps the need to observe and protect those rights in place when paragraph 2 or 3 is applied. JUST TRUE for paragraph 2 or 3; any other paragraph is not named (NOTHING, silent).
-- src:490 | 5. Paragraphs 2 and 3 are without prejudice to the need to observe and protect intellectual property rights, confidential business information and trade secrets in accordance with Union and national law.
@ref Art 25(5) (src:490)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the paragraph` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 25(5) the need to observe and protect intellectual property rights, confidential business information and trade secrets in accordance with Union and national law remains` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the paragraph` EQUALS 2 OR `the paragraph` EQUALS 3
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the clause names paragraphs 2 and 3 only
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 25, "", 0)
